A||||9||Gokart||Power locks||||5||
Z||000000||Gokart||02-16-2000||02:41 PM||||Anyone else that has power locks have to press the unlock or lock 2 or 3 times to get the lock lever over or is my motor going? Maybe needs lubing?||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||02-16-2000||03:09 PM||||Liberal lubing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BOILERMAKER||02-16-2000||03:16 PM||||Get ready to break out the KY ... O, this is the wrong place for that, maybe you should use PB Blaster (or your favorite automotive lubricant) on that problem.<P>Seriously, I had that same exact problem and lubed up all of the pivot points and it works like a charm now.||||reg||1
Z||000003||cobra427||02-16-2000||03:36 PM||||Gok, If you have had to take the door panels off,the thumb lever that you use to manually lock the doors is sometimes a little tricky to take off and equally as tricky to put back on assuming that you intend to reuse the little felt piece. In the process of trying to get that lever off, you may bend that rod a little and if you do, it puts it a little out of alignment and will cause it to drag a little.Hence the 2-3 hits on the lock button.If that rod is not bent then follow previous members post. Lubricate. <BR>Mine still does it. To lazy to fix.||||reg||1
Z||000004||william_thorniii||02-16-2000||03:56 PM||||Gentlemen,<P>Speaking of lubricating the locks... when I did this I did something that I knew that I shouldn't but I did anyway.  I ripped off that paper laminate on the inside of the doors.  I knew that it was to help keep the cold air out, but I said "How much air can paper stop?"  This past winter while on the highway, my left knee would quickly go numb.  It was amazing the amount of air that comes in by those door lock rocker switches!  Does anyone have an easy fixes for this?<P>THX,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000005||Phil||02-16-2000||04:47 PM||||I replaced my vapor barrier with some heavy duty plastic film.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gokart||02-16-2000||07:12 PM||||Thanks guys. I have the panels off now cause I had both door glass replaced today. I'll check out the rod and lube before I put back on. Also removed paper so I'll go with Phil's fix as well. I'm kinda low on KY though so I'll have to go with WD40!||||reg||14
Z||000007||cobra427||02-16-2000||07:33 PM||||GoK, I think a better lube than WD-40 would be a white lithium spray grease. It will last a little longer.WD-40 has a tendancy to dry out quicker and put you back to square one.  Just a thought.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||02-17-2000||12:17 AM||||I need to do this too.. does anyone have any opinions about Triflow?  it's a teflon based lube.. i have a ton of it laying around 'cause i use it for my bike.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Gokart||02-17-2000||04:53 AM||||Thanks Cobra!||||reg||14
